From 9f6104d5557b6b595a468383077f21de3bf77e87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 08:30:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] International Agreement lines were dropped whole: 459 ->
 509 complete, 421 -> 468 exact

`corpus::classify()` had a catch-all treating any line led by a known CARD
NAME as bookkeeping. "International Agreement" is itself a card name, so
`International Agreement Purple takes Kremlin in hand; ...` was discarded
entirely -- the taken card, often a wonder, never entered the hand, and the
later build spend then looked illegal. 15 of the 38 IllegalMove: WonderStep
games traced straight to it.

Three parts:
  * corpus.rs classifies those lines as TakeCard.
  * replay_common.rs walks every `;`-joined pick on the line, applying
    best_age_sibling and calling resolve_intervening once per LINE, grounding
    each pick against the open TakeRow choice own offered slots (these picks
    carry no "uses N civil action" clause, so the generic cost matcher does
    not apply).
  * resolve_intervening TakeRow matching required the card already be present
    in the row by identity -- impossible for a card never seen there before.
    Widened to accept an ungrounded offered slot. Found by two genuine
    regressions the guard bar caught (7522957, 7523114), root-caused before
    landing rather than tolerated.

Guard, full 1011-game sweep against the 459 baseline: ZERO regressions,
50 wins. 509 completed, 468 exact.

Still open, flagged not fixed: `GAME DATA UPDATED` admin-correction lines are
still dropped as bookkeeping (2 games).
