From 71e93f59faa8e4a5e91f870057c0441950b7a500 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 09:11:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Replacing a leader mid-turn clawed back actions already
 spent (509 -> 553 complete)

`apply.rs::h_play_leader` called `on_leave_play`, which decrements
`civil_actions`/`military_actions` (clamped at 0) when a leader carrying a flat
action bonus leaves play. If part of that bonus had ALREADY BEEN SPENT this
turn before the swap, it was subtracted a second time.

Human game 7522520 round 11: Theocracy (3 MA) + Joan of Arc (+1) = 4 MA. Joan
pays 2 MA for a CopyTactic, Isaac Newton replaces her mid-turn, and the human
then builds two more units -- only possible with 2 MA left. The engine had 1
and called the second build illegal.

The fix reuses `carry_over_action_pool`, the already-correct formula
`set_government` uses for the analogous revolution case. No new machinery.

This is not a replayer-only bug: the bot loses actions it legitimately banked
every time it swaps a leader, and wasting a civil action is the worst move in
the game.

Full 1011-game sweep against the frozen 509 baseline: ZERO regressions,
44 wins. 553 completed, 505 exact.

Diagnosed but NOT fixed, with IDs in the notes: `workers_free==0` (31 games),
a peaceful-revolution `no_ca` issue (7), residual resource drift (48), and 3
unresolved.
